Free the tab tint and the popup shade factor

Two gates of the style dialog lock out an input that the style reads.
QtCurveConfig::activeTabAppearanceChanged() sets the tab tint to zero
for the flat and the raised active tab appearance, and
updateEnableStates() then disables the box. The style draws the tint
for both: the four call sites of Style::colorTab() read
opts.colorSelTab alone, and colorTab() never reads the appearance. A
flat active tab with a tint of 100 changes 888 pixels of the notebook
against the same tab with no tint. The raised appearance gives the
same 888.

updateEnableStates() also disables the shade factor of the popup menu
while the shaded popup menu box is ticked and the menubar carries a
shade. Style::setMenuColors() takes the menubar colour as the base in
that state, and then applies the factor on top of it. A factor of 20
changes 10982 pixels of the popup menu, and a factor of 0 changes
10958.

Drop both gates. The tab tint keeps the amount that the user stored.
The gate was the only work of shadePopupMenuChanged(), so the slot now
calls updateChanged(), and the box reports its change like each
neighbouring box.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 10 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

